  "question": {
    "text": "The electric field at point $\\mathrm{p}$ due to an electric dipole is $\\mathrm{E}$. The electric field at point $\\mathrm{R}$ on equitorial line will be $\\frac{\\mathrm{E}}{x}$. The value of $x$ :\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/PmIWB2gnL-hWbIj5mkwDF_6mFsOng3c0VmVGyFTl09Q.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "16",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & E_P=\\frac{2 K P}{r^3}=E \\\\ & E_R=\\frac{K P}{(2 r)^3}=\\frac{E}{16} \\\\ & x=16\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
